# hello.pdf is a hand-built PDF whose xref table stores the BYTE OFFSET of every
# object. Git's default LF -> CRLF conversion on Windows shifts every one of them
# and the file stops parsing — so the fixture must round-trip byte for byte.
*.pdf binary
# Same reason, one step less exotic: a PNG's IDAT stream is deflate, and any
# byte substitution inside it fails the chunk CRC. The extension icons are
# committed, so they have to round-trip exactly.
*.png binary
